#X text 492 100 This patch generates a fibonacci sequence \, sent to its output. It takes a bang to trigger the next step \, and a bang to reset the sequence. I have also used a modulo step to keep the values low so it keeps outputting numbers using the fibonnaci formula as the base (the numbers get too big otherwise \, and it just stops). The actual fibonacci sequence is therefore limited \, but it works as the base. The value of the modulo decides how the sequence transforms., f 88;
#X text 293 398 This part sends the right input to alternating sides \, --> storing two steps of the sequence so they can be added together;
#X text 904 404 <-- The objects holding the two steps of the sequence to be added together. One is initialized to 0 \, the other to 1;
#X obj 822 578 inlet;
#X text 874 577 <-- Inlet for adjusting mod value;
#X text 842 615 <-- The mod value can be changed to mess with the sequence length and steps values beyond the mod point;
